---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import WorkflowAnatomy from "../components/WorkflowAnatomy.astro";
import RiskMeters from "../components/RiskMeters.astro";
import EncodingReader from "../components/EncodingReader.astro";
import BentoAnatomy from "../components/BentoAnatomy.astro";
import "../styles/landing.css";
import "../styles/bento-anatomy.css";
import "../styles/experience.css";

const title = "repyy | A closer look before you run";
const description =
  "Inspect take-home assignments before installing dependencies, starting the project or opening it in your IDE. Repyy reports risks and limitations.";
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} rootClass="landing-root" bodyClass="landing-page">
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero" id="top">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="context-line">Repository preflight. Free and open source.</p>
        <h1>
          A closer look.<span>Before you run.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Repyy reviews unfamiliar take-home repositories before you install dependencies, start the project, or open it in your IDE.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="./demo/">
            View the demo report
          </a>
          <a class="text-link" href="#install">
            Install Repyy <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-limitation">Static analysis can identify risks, but it cannot prove that a repository is safe.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="workflow" id="workflow">
      <div class="workflow-intro">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="section-label">How it works</p>
          <h2>Files in. Evidence out.</h2>
          <p>Start with a local folder or Git URL. Keep assignment-controlled commands unexecuted while you review.</p>
        </div>
        <WorkflowAnatomy />
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="coverage" id="coverage">
      <div class="section-head coverage-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">What the scan checks</p>
          <h2>Look beyond the source files.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Static checks look for patterns across install paths, automation, encoded payloads, credentials, metadata, and archives.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="coverage-grid">
        <article class="coverage-card coverage-primary">
          <div class="card-meta">
            <span>01 / Execution paths</span>
            <strong>Install paths</strong>
          </div>
          <p class="scan-caption">A closer look at the paths that can execute.</p>
          <BentoAnatomy kind="install" />
          <div class="coverage-probe">
            <span>
              <b>package.json</b>
              <small>lifecycle scripts</small>
              <i>2 signals</i>
            </span>
            <span>
              <b>.github/workflows</b>
              <small>automation</small>
              <i>checked</i>
            </span>
            <span>
              <b>.vscode/tasks.json</b>
              <small>editor tasks</small>
              <i>checked</i>
            </span>
            <span>
              <b>fixtures/sample.zip</b>
              <small>archive depth 1</small>
              <i>checked</i>
            </span>
          </div>
          <p>Lifecycle scripts, custom registries, unexpected binaries, and download-to-execute chains are evaluated together.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="coverage-card coverage-confidence">
          <div class="card-meta">
            <span>02 / Finding model</span>
            <strong>Severity ≠ confidence</strong>
          </div>
          <RiskMeters />
          <p>Severity and confidence remain separate so review signals are not presented as proof of compromise.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="coverage-card coverage-signal">
          <div class="card-meta">
            <span>03 / Encoded behavior</span>
            <strong>
              Hidden code.
              <br />
              Visible intent.
            </strong>
          </div>
          <EncodingReader />
          <p>Code can hide what it does behind encoded text. Repyy flags decoding and execution patterns for you to inspect.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="coverage-card coverage-secrets">
          <div class="credentials-copy">
            <div class="card-meta">
              <span>04 / Redacted evidence</span>
              <strong>Credentials</strong>
            </div>
            <div class="redaction" aria-hidden="true">
              <span>ghp_</span>
              <i></i>
              <i></i>
              <i></i>
            </div>
            <p>Recognized credential-shaped values are redacted. Review reports for sensitive content before sharing.</p>
          </div>
          <BentoAnatomy kind="secrets" />
        </article>

        <article class="coverage-card coverage-surface">
          <div class="surface-copy">
            <div class="card-meta">
              <span>05 / Repository surfaces</span>
              <strong>Beyond the app folder</strong>
            </div>
            <p>CI, editor tasks, agent instructions, containers, Git hooks, archives, and social-engineering signals remain in scope.</p>
          </div>
          <BentoAnatomy kind="surface" />
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="limits">
      <div class="limits-heading">
        <h2>Coverage limits</h2>
        <p>Every scan has a boundary. If a timeout, limit, or read error reduces coverage, repyy reports the scan as incomplete.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="limit-grid">
        <div class="limit">
          <strong>10 min</strong>
          <span>Default timeout</span>
        </div>
        <div class="limit">
          <strong>100,000</strong>
          <span>Default file limit</span>
        </div>
        <div class="limit">
          <strong>50 MiB</strong>
          <span>Default per file</span>
        </div>
        <div class="limit">
          <strong>3 levels</strong>
          <span>Archive depth</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="limits-note">These defaults are adjustable. They are not detection guarantees.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="trust-evidence" id="trust" aria-labelledby="trust-title">
      <div class="trust-intro section-head">
        <p class="section-label">Trust, with evidence</p>
        <h2 id="trust-title">
          A clear boundary.
          <br />
          An inspectable tool.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Local scans keep source and reports on your machine. Remote retrieval needs network access. Static analysis can miss malicious behavior and flag
          legitimate code.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="./trust/">
          Read Trust and Limitations ↗
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="evidence-register">
        <a href="./verification/">
          <span class="evidence-number" aria-hidden="true">
            01
          </span>
          <span>
            <strong>Trace the release.</strong>
            <small>Signatures, SBOMs and build provenance. Check which evidence exists for your version.</small>
          </span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <a href="./security-testing/">
          <span class="evidence-number" aria-hidden="true">
            02
          </span>
          <span>
            <strong>Inspect the testing.</strong>
            <small>CodeQL, regression tests and bounded fuzzing, with known gaps documented.</small>
          </span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <a href="./demo/">
          <span class="evidence-number" aria-hidden="true">
            03
          </span>
          <span>
            <strong>Reproduce the results.</strong>
            <small>Inert fixtures, paired controls and visible misses. No universal accuracy claim.</small>
          </span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <div>
          <span class="evidence-number" aria-hidden="true">
            04
          </span>
          <span>
            <strong>Independent review is pending.</strong>
            <small>A prepared scope is available. No external audit is claimed.</small>
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="reports" id="outputs">
      <div class="report-lab" data-report-lab>
        <div class="report-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="section-label">Report formats</p>
            <h2>The same evidence. A view that fits.</h2>
            <p>
              Read it in your terminal, pass it to automation, or keep an offline report. Recognized sensitive values are redacted. Review the report before
              sharing.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="report-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Report formats">
            <button class="is-active" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-report-format="terminal">
              Terminal
            </button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-report-format="json">
              JSON
            </button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-report-format="sarif">
              SARIF
            </button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-report-format="html">
              HTML
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="report-screen">
          <div class="report-screen-bar">
            <span>
              <i></i>
              <i></i>
              <i></i>
            </span>
            <strong data-report-title>Terminal review</strong>
            <button type="button" class="copy-button light" data-report-copy>
              Copy command
            </button>
          </div>
          <pre><code data-report-preview><span class="code-muted">$</span> repyy scan ./assignment

<b>REVIEW REQUIRED</b>
2 findings need context

HIGH  PKG-001   package.json:12
MED   OBFS-003   src/setup.js:48</code></pre>
        </div>
        <aside class="report-notes">
          <p class="section-label">Abbreviated format examples</p>
          <div>
            <strong data-report-use>Human review</strong>
            <p data-report-description>Prioritized findings with context and a clear verdict.</p>
          </div>
          <code data-report-command>repyy scan ./assignment</code>
          <a href="./docs/#reports-docs">
            Report reference <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <div class="sample-invitation">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">See it before installing</p>
          <h3>See the report before you install.</h3>
          <p>Explore 11 inert risk examples and their paired controls, scanned with the 0.6.0 preview code.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button primary" href="./demo/">
          Open the demo ↗
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="report-limitation">
        No relevant findings does not prove safety. <a href="./trust/#incomplete-scans-and-exit-codes">Understand statuses and incomplete coverage ↗</a>
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="install" id="install">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="section-label">Get started</p>
        <h2>Start with a scan.</h2>
        <p>Install repyy. Scan the assignment. Review what comes back.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="install-panel" data-install-tabs>
        <div class="install-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Installation methods">
          <button class="is-active" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-install-command="brew install --cask Kevin-Umali/tap/repyy">
            Homebrew
          </button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-install-command="scoop install repyy/repyy">
            Scoop
          </button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-install-command="go install github.com/Kevin-Umali/repyy/cmd/repyy@latest">
            Go
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="install-command">
          <code>
            <span>$</span> <b data-install-output>brew install --cask Kevin-Umali/tap/repyy</b>
          </code>
          <button class="install-copy-button" data-install-copy type="button">
            <span data-copy-label>Copy command</span>
            <i class="copy-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="copy-icon-default">↗</span>
              <span class="copy-icon-success">✓</span>
            </i>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="install-links">
        <a href="./installation/">Installation guide ↗</a>
        <a href="./verification/">Verify your download ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="faq" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
      <h2 id="questions-title">Before you begin.</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>Does “No findings” mean the repository is safe?</summary>
          <p>No. It means the completed scan matched no enabled rule. Static analysis can miss malicious behavior and can report harmless code.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I scan private repositories?</summary>
          <p>Yes. HTTPS clones can use supported provider tokens. SSH remotes use your existing SSH agent.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can a repository weaken its own scan?</summary>
          <p>No. Repository-owned .repyy.yaml files are ignored. Pass a configuration file you trust with the --config flag.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import "../scripts/site.js";
  import "../scripts/landing.js";
</script>
